# C# conventions

Auto-attaches only inside C# files, so this guidance never leaks into non-C# nodes.
(This is an example of the Cursor-native scoping layer described in `AGENTS.md`.)

- Prefer clear, self-documenting names over comments.
- Use file-scoped namespaces and modern C# features where they aid readability.
- Keep demo code minimal: show the concept, avoid unrelated abstractions.
- One public concept per file where practical.
- Include a short usage example (test, `Program.cs`, or README snippet) so the node runs.
